et` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total. Between attempts it waits `backoff \u00d7 2^(attempt\u22121)` seconds, which is 0.5s and then 1s by default.\n\n- **What gets retried:** only an `HTTPError` with code 503. Any other HTTP error is raised right away. If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised to the caller. Each discarded 503 response is closed before the next attempt.\n- **New settings:** two optional constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`. Existing calls work unchanged.\n- **Not retried:** network failures such as timeouts or refused connections. I left these alone because you asked about 503 only.\n\nI checked it against a local HTTP server, using a 0.01s backoff to keep it quick:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | returns the JSON | 3 |\n| 503, 503, 503 | raises HTTPError 503 | 3 |\n| 500 | raises HTTPError 500 | 1 |\n| 200 | returns the JSON | 1 |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add any tests.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34695, "requests_cache_write": 143547, "requests_cost_usd": 0.758462, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1687, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial8", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 75, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:48:08.398742+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 21.318, "t_checker_s": 2.378, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured",